<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Finland (1918)</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Helsinki</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived attempt to make independent Finland a monarchy under a German prince, abandoned when Germany lost the First World War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the civil war, conservative politicians wanted a strong monarchy tied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, whose troops had helped the Whites win. On 9 October 1918 a rump parliament, without the Social Democrats, elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-charles-of-hesse">Prince Frederick Charles of Hesse</a> as king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pehr-evind-svinhufvud">Pehr Evind Svinhufvud</a> served as regent.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom existed largely on paper. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-charles-of-hesse">Frederick Charles</a> never came to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>, and no coronation took place. German influence over the army and the economy was strong, and the monarchists hoped the throne would secure German protection against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> defeat in November 1918 made a German king impossible. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-charles-of-hesse">Frederick Charles</a> renounced the throne on 14 December 1918, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-gustaf-emil-mannerheim">Mannerheim</a> replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pehr-evind-svinhufvud">Svinhufvud</a> as regent. The constitution of 1919 created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Republic of Finland</a>, and the monarchy project was abandoned.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-finland-1918.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Finland (1918)" width="320" height="196"><figcaption>Image: Original design by Eero Snellman, vectorised by Oraivio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Finland_1918-1920_(State).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Helsinki</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick Charles of Hesse, Pehr Evind Svinhufvud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Finnish, Swedish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/finland">Finland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Finland, Suomen kuningaskunta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=kingdom-of-finland-1918" aria-label="Kingdom of Finland (1918) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5201 163 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Finland (1918) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5521 419L5521 419M5521 419L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 419h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5521 419h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5521 419h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Helsinki. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=kingdom-of-finland-1918">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
